<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model & Lewis's law epithelial packing — MorphoEval overall 91.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py` (90.9/100, up from 57.7/100 in Pass 1; +33.2 points). The remediated script implements the full Farhadifar et al. (2007) apical vertex energy functional, classifies the 2D `(Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar)` ground-state phase diagram across Cases I, II, and III, simulates all 4 mechanical/developmental regimes (proliferating larval wing disc `P(6)=0.440, r=0.9820`, annealed pupal wing `P(6)=0.840, mu_2=0.160`, high-contractility cortex `Gamma_bar=0.10`, and soft Case II network `Lambda_bar=-0.25`), models UV laser adherens-junction ablation recoil (`v_0 = 0.22 um/s`), segments the SHA-256-locked apical junction-stained epithelial specimen (`drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg`, `N=37` cells, `P(n)` Pearson `r = 0.9913`), and is backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_043_drosophila_wing_vertex_model.lean`. Overall 91.0/100 (faithfulness 90.4, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py at b9976f8, image/png, 977473 B, 3075×1290 px, artifact_sha256 d1c94b16e8a8dabd2fa188b59f66091e4dd352b73f3ec1401c0579b6e896bbf1 (sha256 d1c94b16e8a8dabd2fa188b59f66091e4dd352b73f3ec1401c0579b6e896bbf1), spec_fingerprint 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52; artifact_sha256: d1c94b16e8a8dabd2fa188b59f66091e4dd352b73f3ec1401c0579b6e896bbf1. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse). | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 (mu_2 = 0.765) and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78 (mu_2 = 0.250).; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic apical vertex packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 mechanical regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, and Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep. | Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (`drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg`, N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells.; does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature or 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D apical vertex network to an explicit planar cell polarity (PCP) Frizzled/Strabismus edge-asymmetry tensor on individual bonds to model anisotropic wing-blade elongation during pupal hinge contraction." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

